 "note": "div and sqrt built by conformance/exact_ops.py from this oracle's own decode and encode. Written under _exact when pass 210 found the silicon-sprint packs of the same name carried different goldens and left open which was right. Pass 232 settled it: those goldens came from conformance/golden_conformance_vectors.py, a float32 proxy whose decoder zeroes subnormal mantissas, encodes NaN as +0 and returns -Inf for 0/0. The silicon-sprint packs have been recomputed from the same oracles as this one, so the two no longer disagree. DIVERGES FROM specs/numeric/gf16.t27 IN TWO WAYS, and the difference is in the expected values here: (1) the spec declares GF16_NAN = 0xFE01, with the sign bit set, while this oracle builds a quiet NaN family-generically as (exp_max << mant_bits) | 1 = 0x7E01; (2) the spec flushes subnormals to zero, this oracle uses gradual underflow. A spec-conformant design therefore disagrees with these vectors on those inputs and is not thereby wrong. Measured 2026-08-11: three independently stored copies of gf16_mul.v each produced exactly 110 mismatches out of 994 against this pack -- 55 NaN sign, 13 flushed subnormals, 4 one-LSB, 38 other.",
